            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# Kiki 0.4.3

This release sharpens Kiki’s visual identity and makes navigation clearer in both appearances.

## What’s improved

- Orange is now Kiki’s primary interaction color across buttons, feature accents, selection states, and transcription surfaces.
- Light Mode selections use a stronger warm highlight that is easy to distinguish from the surrounding interface.
- Dark Mode selections use a coordinated warm surface with clear contrast.
- Sidebar navigation now spans the full available row and uses deliberate horizontal padding around every icon and label.
- The welcome screen now says: “Designed around speed, privacy, and the way you actually work.”
- The Accent Color preference now labels Kiki’s default accent as Orange.

Transcription, performance, and Kiki’s fully local privacy model remain unchanged.
]]></description>
